<title>USA: Court denies motion to stop Chateau buyback.</title>
<headline>Court denies motion to stop Chateau buyback.</headline>
<dateline>CLINTON TOWNSHIP, Mich. 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chateau Properties Inc said on Thursday the court denied a motion by Manufactured Home Communities Inc to stop Chateau from proceeding with its plan to repurchase up to 1.45 million of its outstanding common shares.</p>
<p>Chateau said the U.S. District Court for the District of Maryland, Northern Division denied the motion for a temporary restraining order.</p>
<p>On September 18 Chateau and ROC Communities Inc said their boards of directors had approved a revised merger agreement, which included a programme through which Chateau would repurchase up to 1.45 million of the approximately 6.1 million shares of the company's common stock outstanding.</p>
<p>The original merger deal between the companies was announced in July.</p>
<p>Manufactured Homes made a competing bid to acquire Chateau in August that was rebuffed.</p>
